# SPA Corp — Coding Style

**Project type:** Corporate profile (NOT e-commerce). Keep structure lean — no unused wrappers.

## Folder layout

```
src/
├── app/[locale]/page.tsx      # Composes home sections
├── components/
│   ├── about/                 # WhoWeAre (counters inline)
│   ├── home/                  # Hero, Services, Why, WhyCards, Sectors, IsoBanner, Partners
│   ├── layout/header|footer/
│   └── ui/                    # Button, Reveal, Section, HeaderSection, CountUp
├── i18n/
├── lib/api/ + lib/data/ + theme.ts + motion.ts
└── styles/globals.css
messages/{ar,en}/
```

## Data flow

```
lib/data/*.json → lib/api/*.ts → home|about/*.tsx (fetch + compose)
```

No thin wrapper files. One section file does fetch + render when possible.

## When to split a file

Prefer **one file per section**. Split only when:

1. File would exceed ~100–150 lines, **or**
2. You need a clear `"use client"` boundary (motion/interaction) while the parent stays a Server Component

Example: `Why.tsx` (server fetch) + `WhyCards.tsx` (client cards) is fine.  
Do **not** extract tiny pieces like `CounterCard.tsx` / `ServiceCard.tsx` into their own files — keep them as local functions in the section.

## Rules

- Server Components by default; `"use client"` only for motion, theme toggle, scroll/menu
- Shared UI in `components/ui/` — never invent parallel systems
- Do not add empty folders (`store/`, `providers/`, `actions/`) until needed
- Theme init = inline script in layout; toggle logic in `lib/theme.ts`
- No ThemeProvider / ThemeScript components
